##! experimental { givens }

// =====================================================================
//  DRIVE_GAMES — narrow the drive model to a handful of games
//
//  The drive model runs three season-wide window-function passes before
//  any query sees a row: dropping the feed's duplicate drives, counting
//  possessions left, and repairing the running score. Every one of them
//  partitions by game, so restricting the rows to a few games FIRST gives
//  exactly the same answers for those games — over a few hundred drives
//  instead of the whole season's.
//
//  The games reports set it when they fetch drive charts for the games on
//  screen. Everything else leaves it empty, which filters nothing.
//
//  Declared in its own file, with no imports, because drives.malloy
//  applies it and everything else imports drives.malloy.
// =====================================================================

given:

  #(doc) Game ids to restrict the drive data to before the season-wide passes run, for example 401752677, 401754512. Empty (the default) means every game. Set by the games reports when they fetch drive charts; not a reader-facing control.
  # label="Drive chart games"
  DRIVE_GAMES :: filter<number> is f''
